Now the right part of the inequality: x/5 < 6/7. Again, multiply both sides by 5. So, x < (6/7)*5. Let me calculate that. 6*5 is 30, so 30/7. Dividing 30 by 7 gives approximately 4.2857. So, x has to be less than about 4.2857.

Putting both together, x has to be greater than 10/3 (which is roughly 3.333) and less than 30/7 (approximately 4.2857). Since x has to be an integer, the possible values for x would be integers between 3.333 and 4.2857. The integers in that interval are 4, right? Because 4 is greater than 3.333 and less than 4.2857. 

