   $$

2. Then, the same quarters are stacked and divided into piles of 7, resulting in 5 left over. Similarly, this means:
   $$
   q \equiv 5 \pmod{7}
   $$

We are looking for a number $ q $ that satisfies both of these congruences. To find such a number, we can use the Chinese Remainder Theorem (CRT), which helps find a number that satisfies a system of simultaneous congruences with coprime moduli.

